*Note: Commission ratio (IGAAP) is omitted from the table above as this figure was not separately disclosed as a standalone ratio in either the statutory filing or the investor deck for H1FY26.*

## Key Notes & Discrepancy Flags

### GWP Basis Selection
Per the 1/n (statutory) basis preference, the reported Total GWP of **₹3,475.0 Cr** and Retail Health GWP of **₹2,371.8 Cr** reflect the "with 1/n" figures. The deck also separately discloses "without 1/n" figures (₹3,982.7 Cr and ₹2,809.9 Cr respectively), which were deliberately excluded per the sourcing rules. Effective October 1, 2024, long-term products are accounted for on a 1/n basis per IRDAI mandate — this makes H1FY26 figures on this basis **not directly comparable** to pre-FY25 reporting periods.

### NWP Reconciliation
The raw statutory filing table contained an OCR/formatting anomaly (garbled column headers reading "September 30, 20202025"), producing an inconsistent NWP figure of ₹347.45 Cr. The Investor Presentation's clean KPI table shows NWP = **₹2,737.9 Cr**, which is internally consistent when cross-checked: GWP (₹3,475.0 Cr) × Retention Ratio (78.8%) ≈ ₹2,738 Cr. The Investor Presentation figure was therefore used as the more reliable statutory-basis value.

### Profit After Tax — IGAAP vs. IFRS Divergence
There is a notable divergence between the IGAAP PAT (**-₹126.7 Cr**, a loss) and the IFRS PAT (**+₹131.72 Cr**, a profit) for the same H1FY26 period. This reflects differing treatment of items such as premium recognition, reserving methodology, and other GAAP-to-IFRS adjustment items between the two accounting frameworks — both figures are statutory/audited as filed and are not comparable on a like-for-like basis.

### Investment Yield — Annualized vs. Period Figure
The Investor Presentation reports Investment Yield as **7.3%** on an annualized basis, while the underlying statutory filing shows a non-annualized "Yield on Investments (without unrealized gains), Year to date" figure of 3.64% for the same six-month period. The annualized figure (7.3%) has been reported per the headline KPI convention used in the investor deck.

### Commission Ratio — Not Disclosed
Commission ratio (IGAAP) as a standalone percentage was not disclosed in either the statutory filing or the investor presentation for H1FY26. The statutory filing shows only the absolute net commission figure (₹53,964 Lakhs, year-to-date) without a corresponding ratio to premium. This has been left blank rather than estimated, per instructions.</ans>
